WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.387 --> 00:00:01.707
- You always have to fight for things

00:00:01.707 --> 00:00:02.540
that are worth it.

00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:03.388
So boring.

00:00:03.388 --> 00:00:04.626
Everyone's doing the same thing.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.831
Are you walking the dog,

00:00:05.831 --> 00:00:07.254
or is the dog walking you?

00:00:07.254 --> 00:00:08.797
The more brilliant people
that you hang around

00:00:08.797 --> 00:00:10.147
the more inspired you get.

00:00:10.147 --> 00:00:12.071
We're living in an age, in a society now,

00:00:12.071 --> 00:00:15.248
where that is almost
looked at as a weakness.

00:00:15.248 --> 00:00:17.231
You turn the apple cart
over and then what?

00:00:17.231 --> 00:00:18.328
Then everyone's looking at an apple cart

00:00:18.328 --> 00:00:19.370
that's turned over and they're like,

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:20.616
well now what do I do?

00:00:20.616 --> 00:00:22.615
In my mind, there's a little movie playing

00:00:22.615 --> 00:00:25.237
and I always envision
scenarios and characters.

00:00:25.237 --> 00:00:27.328
You could never compare, you know,

00:00:27.328 --> 00:00:28.582
Picasso with Leger

00:00:28.582 --> 00:00:29.415
I always tell people,

00:00:29.415 --> 00:00:32.294
vacations are for people
who don't like their job.

00:00:32.294 --> 00:00:33.809
I want to conquer the world.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.639
- She's an American singer, songwriter,

00:00:35.639 --> 00:00:37.420
actress, and business woman.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:39.957
- She pushed the boundaries
in her music and videos.

00:00:39.957 --> 00:00:42.412
- She sold over 300 million records

00:00:42.412 --> 00:00:44.399
and she is the world's best selling

00:00:44.399 --> 00:00:46.683
female recording artist of all time.

00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:47.712
- She's Madonna,

00:00:47.712 --> 00:00:49.811
and here are her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:49.811 --> 00:00:52.728
(rocket exploding)

00:00:55.395 --> 00:00:57.678
- I think the best
advice I can give anyone

00:00:57.678 --> 00:00:59.526
male or female, is that, you know,

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:03.239
you have to really believe
in what you're doing.

00:01:03.239 --> 00:01:05.712
I think having a good job

00:01:05.712 --> 00:01:07.295
and having work is,

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.302
it's hard to come by

00:01:11.983 --> 00:01:14.387
and being able to do what you
want to do with your life.

00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:17.548
You have to be willing, first of all,

00:01:17.548 --> 00:01:19.994
you have to be really passionate

00:01:19.994 --> 00:01:22.483
about what you do and really
believe in what you do,

00:01:22.483 --> 00:01:24.025
'cause there's going to be a lot of fights

00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:25.653
and battles and struggles along the way,

00:01:25.653 --> 00:01:27.003
so my best advice is to

00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:30.068
really believe and love what you do.

00:01:30.068 --> 00:01:33.235
(audience applauding)

00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:36.887
Because a the end of the day,

00:01:36.887 --> 00:01:38.387
nothing, you know,

00:01:39.915 --> 00:01:41.966
you always have to fight for things

00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:43.159
that are worth it.

00:01:43.159 --> 00:01:45.547
Put your boxing gloves on.

00:01:45.547 --> 00:01:46.993
- [Interviewer] Will we
ever see choreography

00:01:46.993 --> 00:01:49.743
in a video again, meter, dancing?

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:52.750
- It's possible.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.232
It's just that I got so sick

00:01:54.232 --> 00:01:55.607
of all the videos everybody's making

00:01:55.607 --> 00:01:57.840
where there's like, the troupe of dancers

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.258
and the singer standing in front of it

00:01:59.258 --> 00:02:00.686
and everybody was moving in unison,

00:02:00.686 --> 00:02:02.127
I thought, so boring.

00:02:02.127 --> 00:02:03.496
Everyone's doing the same thing.

00:02:03.496 --> 00:02:06.743
I wanted to get away from all of that

00:02:06.743 --> 00:02:10.446
but, yeah, I could see
doing something like that.

00:02:10.446 --> 00:02:13.600
Actually, because now, not
so many people are doing it,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.927
so be something different.

00:02:15.927 --> 00:02:17.115
- You will definitely always

00:02:17.115 --> 00:02:19.543
go against the grain, won't you?

00:02:19.543 --> 00:02:23.932
- Well, I will always take
the road less traveled by.

00:02:23.932 --> 00:02:25.388
We're all controlled by our ego.

00:02:25.388 --> 00:02:26.589
We're all slaves to our ego.

00:02:26.589 --> 00:02:28.919
Everything we do is about our ego.

00:02:28.919 --> 00:02:29.752
- Guilty as charged.

00:02:29.752 --> 00:02:30.807
- Absolutely and so am I,

00:02:30.807 --> 00:02:32.019
and so are we all.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:35.324
If I didn't have a huge
ego, I wouldn't be here.

00:02:35.324 --> 00:02:36.667
At a certain point,

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:39.338
you have to understand
that it is, you know,

00:02:39.338 --> 00:02:42.248
it's your dog and it's like,

00:02:42.248 --> 00:02:43.792
are you walking the dog

00:02:43.792 --> 00:02:45.074
or is the dog walking you?

00:02:45.074 --> 00:02:47.753
The best way to be inspired as an artist

00:02:47.753 --> 00:02:50.095
is to be around humanity.

00:02:50.095 --> 00:02:51.548
Whether you're walking down the street,

00:02:51.548 --> 00:02:55.303
or you're standing in the
middle of a shopping mall,

00:02:55.303 --> 00:02:59.470
or you're hanging around a lot
of really brilliant people.

00:03:00.638 --> 00:03:03.682
I mean, you know, the smarter,

00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:05.798
I mean, the more brilliant people

00:03:05.798 --> 00:03:06.631
that you hang around,

00:03:06.631 --> 00:03:09.631
the more inspired you get, you know.

00:03:11.432 --> 00:03:14.353
I just like to be around talented people,

00:03:14.353 --> 00:03:17.741
whether I use what I learned
from them in my work or not.

00:03:17.741 --> 00:03:18.787
I always say to myself,

00:03:18.787 --> 00:03:20.723
why aren't people inspired

00:03:20.723 --> 00:03:22.263
by everything that I've accomplished?

00:03:22.263 --> 00:03:24.367
Why is everybody afraid?

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.562
You know, I think my strength,

00:03:25.562 --> 00:03:28.661
and that's like, the hardest thing

00:03:28.661 --> 00:03:31.540
that I've had to sort of grasp and accept

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:35.037
is that my surviving, and my strength,

00:03:35.037 --> 00:03:37.891
and the things that I've accomplished,

00:03:37.891 --> 00:03:41.311
isn't inspirational to other people.

00:03:41.311 --> 00:03:43.537
It's frightening, I think.

00:03:43.537 --> 00:03:45.119
I think it's because

00:03:45.119 --> 00:03:48.611
so many people are so afraid to,

00:03:48.611 --> 00:03:49.958
to have a point of view,

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:51.450
to strike out on their own,

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:54.471
and to try and realize
one of their dreams.

00:03:54.471 --> 00:03:55.754
To see someone else doing it,

00:03:55.754 --> 00:03:58.832
we're living in an age, in a society now,

00:03:58.832 --> 00:04:02.362
where that is almost
looked at as a weakness,

00:04:02.362 --> 00:04:03.938
something to be ashamed of.

00:04:03.938 --> 00:04:05.077
- [Interviewer] Most
people are immobilized

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.630
by the fear of failure.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.509
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:04:08.509 --> 00:04:10.189
When they see someone
else doing really well,

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:11.865
it's like, I think,

00:04:11.865 --> 00:04:13.845
deep down inside, it's human nature,

00:04:13.845 --> 00:04:14.931
to want to destroy them,

00:04:14.931 --> 00:04:15.950
to try to destroy them,

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:18.119
to try to bring them down to your level

00:04:18.119 --> 00:04:20.359
so you can feel good about yourself.

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.423
- You have done a really
good job, though, I think,

00:04:23.423 --> 00:04:25.260
of making the rest of us

00:04:25.260 --> 00:04:26.613
think you don't care very much

00:04:26.613 --> 00:04:27.658
what other people think.

00:04:27.658 --> 00:04:28.704
- I'm a good actress.

00:04:28.704 --> 00:04:30.323
(Madonna laughing)

00:04:30.323 --> 00:04:32.118
I mean, I'm a rebel,

00:04:32.118 --> 00:04:34.537
and, you know, that's
the stance of a rebel.

00:04:34.537 --> 00:04:36.520
The stance of a rebel is, you know,

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:39.861
I can't say bad words
on T.V. but, you know,

00:04:39.861 --> 00:04:41.256
I don't care what you think.

00:04:41.256 --> 00:04:44.162
If it's just for the sake
of upsetting the apple cart,

00:04:44.162 --> 00:04:45.247
you're not really helping people.

00:04:45.247 --> 00:04:47.513
You turn the apple cart
over and then what?

00:04:47.513 --> 00:04:49.004
Then everyone's looking at an apple cart

00:04:49.004 --> 00:04:49.863
that's turned over and they're like,

00:04:49.863 --> 00:04:51.157
well, now what do I do?

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.021
- So, you've done a little of that,

00:04:52.021 --> 00:04:52.854
- God, yeah.
- just for the sake of it.

00:04:52.854 --> 00:04:54.841
- Just for the sake of it.

00:04:54.841 --> 00:04:56.313
- When I write music,

00:04:56.313 --> 00:04:58.147
I like to write them, like,

00:04:58.147 --> 00:05:00.031
in my mind there's a little movie playing.

00:05:00.031 --> 00:05:02.620
I always envision
scenarios and characters,

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:03.453
and of course,

00:05:03.453 --> 00:05:05.952
it's not always something
that I've experienced,

00:05:05.952 --> 00:05:08.337
but I always say it in the first person,

00:05:08.337 --> 00:05:09.385
so it becomes,

00:05:09.385 --> 00:05:11.977
it seems like it's a personal thing.

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.609
They're just usually ideas that amuse me.

00:05:14.609 --> 00:05:16.368
I mean, sometimes they're things

00:05:16.368 --> 00:05:17.392
that I think are erotic.

00:05:17.392 --> 00:05:19.343
Sometimes they're things that I think

00:05:19.343 --> 00:05:21.787
would be interesting
to write a song about,

00:05:21.787 --> 00:05:23.586
because no one's ever
written a song about it.

00:05:23.586 --> 00:05:24.524
You know, I mean,

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:26.212
I'm influenced by many things

00:05:26.212 --> 00:05:28.433
and my inspirations come
from lots of different places

00:05:28.433 --> 00:05:29.644
and sometimes I know

00:05:29.644 --> 00:05:31.727
I'm purposely being funny

00:05:33.357 --> 00:05:35.024
or ironic, you know.

00:05:36.366 --> 00:05:40.081
Sometimes I just like the
way words sound, I mean.

00:05:40.081 --> 00:05:41.118
I just think that people,

00:05:41.118 --> 00:05:45.331
it's pointless for people to
get into a creative arena,

00:05:45.331 --> 00:05:47.196
and say, I want to be the best.

00:05:47.196 --> 00:05:48.029
- Yeah.

00:05:48.029 --> 00:05:48.990
- I mean, you know,

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:51.867
there are, everyone has what they have.

00:05:51.867 --> 00:05:53.051
They say what they say

00:05:53.051 --> 00:05:55.502
and you could never compare, you know,

00:05:55.502 --> 00:05:56.864
Picasso with Leger.

00:05:56.864 --> 00:06:00.281
Everybody has something different to say.

00:06:04.374 --> 00:06:06.147
It's silly to get in there and say,

00:06:06.147 --> 00:06:07.695
my brush stroke is better
than another person's.

00:06:07.695 --> 00:06:08.528
- Yeah.

00:06:08.528 --> 00:06:10.678
- You know, it's better to say,

00:06:10.678 --> 00:06:12.129
am I being true to myself

00:06:12.129 --> 00:06:13.562
and is this what I want to say

00:06:13.562 --> 00:06:16.491
and have I expressed myself, you know,

00:06:16.491 --> 00:06:18.215
the way I want to express myself?

00:06:18.215 --> 00:06:19.048
- Yeah.

00:06:19.048 --> 00:06:20.604
- That's what it's all about.

00:06:20.604 --> 00:06:22.261
- Would you, are you trying to,

00:06:22.261 --> 00:06:25.525
would you like to find another Madonna?

00:06:25.525 --> 00:06:27.012
- Well, I don't think that's possible.

00:06:27.012 --> 00:06:27.845
(Madonna laughing)

00:06:27.845 --> 00:06:30.678
What I'm trying to find is really,

00:06:32.446 --> 00:06:33.279
I don't know,

00:06:33.279 --> 00:06:34.859
fresh talent that's saying something,

00:06:34.859 --> 00:06:36.359
cutting edge, new.

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:40.185
I mean we found some really good groups.

00:06:40.185 --> 00:06:41.646
We've signed a couple groups so far

00:06:41.646 --> 00:06:43.510
and I'm really excited about them.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.532
- This obviously is going to mean

00:06:44.532 --> 00:06:45.982
more work for you, presumably.

00:06:45.982 --> 00:06:48.812
- It is already more work for me.

00:06:48.812 --> 00:06:50.052
- I'm not saying it's perfect

00:06:50.052 --> 00:06:51.355
but some people, perhaps,

00:06:51.355 --> 00:06:52.635
would think if they had that much success,

00:06:52.635 --> 00:06:53.671
if they had that much wealth,

00:06:53.671 --> 00:06:54.973
maybe one thing they'd want to do,

00:06:54.973 --> 00:06:56.685
is while they were still
young enough to enjoy it,

00:06:56.685 --> 00:06:57.860
is maybe take a year off,

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.021
kick around the world, you know,

00:06:59.021 --> 00:07:00.339
go fishing, whatever.

00:07:00.339 --> 00:07:01.599
- I enjoy what I do.

00:07:01.599 --> 00:07:03.554
I mean, life is short

00:07:03.554 --> 00:07:04.799
and I have lots of things to do

00:07:04.799 --> 00:07:06.190
and I see talent out there

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.458
and I want to do something with it.

00:07:09.458 --> 00:07:11.514
I like watching, I like planting seeds

00:07:11.514 --> 00:07:13.515
and watching it grow,
you know what I mean?

00:07:13.515 --> 00:07:14.840
It's inspiring.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:17.034
- Do you actually take a holiday off?

00:07:17.034 --> 00:07:18.617
- Mm. What is that?

00:07:19.739 --> 00:07:21.061
I always tell people,

00:07:21.061 --> 00:07:24.348
vacations are for people
who don't like their job.

00:07:24.348 --> 00:07:25.952
I like what I do.

00:07:25.952 --> 00:07:28.202
- What I would like to ultimately achieve,

00:07:28.202 --> 00:07:30.384
I already told Dick Clark once

00:07:30.384 --> 00:07:31.895
on American Bandstand,

00:07:31.895 --> 00:07:34.127
so I'll repeat it again,

00:07:34.127 --> 00:07:38.294
and annoy everyone who was
annoyed before when I said it,

00:07:39.892 --> 00:07:42.143
I want to conquer the world.

00:07:42.143 --> 00:07:44.856
(Madonna laughing)

00:07:44.856 --> 00:07:46.119
- Thank you so much for watching us.

00:07:46.119 --> 00:07:48.878
We made this video because
Anna Young asked us to.

00:07:48.878 --> 00:07:50.404
If there's someone else

00:07:50.404 --> 00:07:51.794
that you'd like us to profile,

00:07:51.794 --> 00:07:53.282
please leave it in the comments

00:07:53.282 --> 00:07:54.630
and we'll see what we can do.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:55.570
- We'd also love to know

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:57.314
which one of Madonna's top 10 rules

00:07:57.314 --> 00:07:58.819
meant the most to you.

00:07:58.819 --> 00:08:00.292
Leave it in the comments below

00:08:00.292 --> 00:08:01.440
and we'll join the discussion.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.528
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:08:02.528 --> 00:08:05.749
Continue to believe
and we'll see you soon.

00:08:05.749 --> 00:08:08.666
(rocket exploding)

00:08:11.895 --> 00:08:13.958
- My Kabbala teacher, one
of them, used to say to me,

00:08:13.958 --> 00:08:15.339
when in doubt, act like God.

00:08:15.339 --> 00:08:17.753
Then you think, well what does that mean?

00:08:17.753 --> 00:08:19.812
It's like, describe God.

00:08:19.812 --> 00:08:23.305
God would be compassionate, unconditional,

00:08:23.305 --> 00:08:25.243
all-giving, all-loving,

00:08:25.243 --> 00:08:26.547
so, when in doubt,

00:08:26.547 --> 00:08:27.671
behave that way.

00:08:27.671 --> 00:08:28.980
You'll never go wrong.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:30.314
- [Interviewer] Do you
like being powerful,

00:08:30.314 --> 00:08:31.211
do you like power?

00:08:31.211 --> 00:08:32.378
- Who doesn't?

00:08:33.702 --> 00:08:34.535
- Not everybody.

00:08:34.535 --> 00:08:36.024
Do you like--
- Name one person

00:08:36.024 --> 00:08:37.175
who doesn't like power.

00:08:37.175 --> 00:08:38.762
- Everybody wants to be famous.

00:08:38.762 --> 00:08:40.298
- No it's not just fame.

00:08:40.298 --> 00:08:43.594
Power is, anyone can have power.

00:08:43.594 --> 00:08:46.244
It's how you feel about yourself.

00:08:46.244 --> 00:08:48.011
It's how you carry yourself.

00:08:48.011 --> 00:08:49.160
It's the effect that you have on people.

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:50.251
It doesn't necessarily,

00:08:50.251 --> 00:08:52.960
it's not synonymous with fame.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:54.043
I think that,

00:08:55.996 --> 00:08:58.576
I don't think you would find a human being

00:08:58.576 --> 00:09:01.414
on this Earth that wasn't
interested in power.

00:09:01.414 --> 00:09:02.606
I think that two years ago,

00:09:02.606 --> 00:09:04.120
I wasn't really sure why,

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:06.623
what I was on this Earth for.

00:09:06.623 --> 00:09:08.840
I think I was mostly concerned with

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.263
getting things for myself.

00:09:10.263 --> 00:09:11.113
- [Interviewer] Mm hmm.

00:09:11.113 --> 00:09:12.019
- You know, more clothes,

00:09:12.019 --> 00:09:14.509
more money, more popularity,

00:09:14.509 --> 00:09:18.050
more approval, more
boyfriends, more every.

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:21.467
It's just like, I wasn't really thinking,

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:23.609
I was just doing,

00:09:23.609 --> 00:09:26.334
- Mm hmm. So not living
consciously really?

00:09:26.334 --> 00:09:27.167
- Yeah.

00:09:27.167 --> 00:09:28.000
- Yeah.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:31.265
- I think I probably had
some conscious moments.

00:09:31.265 --> 00:09:32.098
- Right.

00:09:32.098 --> 00:09:33.645
- I don't think I was,
like, brain dead, but,

00:09:33.645 --> 00:09:35.499
(audience laughing)

00:09:35.499 --> 00:09:36.680
but--

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.347
- But you know what I mean
not living consciously,

00:09:38.347 --> 00:09:39.659
like a lot of people are just kind of

00:09:39.659 --> 00:09:40.563
going through the motions

00:09:40.563 --> 00:09:41.928
no matter what the motions are.

00:09:41.928 --> 00:09:42.761
- You can't do that.

00:09:42.761 --> 00:09:43.594
- Yeah.

00:09:43.594 --> 00:09:45.353
- No, I think I just
kind of woke up and said,

00:09:45.353 --> 00:09:46.930
okay, what am I on this Earth for?

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:48.461
Why are we all on this Earth for?

00:09:48.461 --> 00:09:49.916
We're here to love.

00:09:49.916 --> 00:09:51.092
We're here to share.

00:09:51.092 --> 00:09:51.925
That's it.

00:09:51.925 --> 00:09:53.540
